{
  "schema": "delve.art.tiles.v1",
  "description": "Maps level tile roles (floor, wall, water, door, ceiling) into texture atlases staged under the gitignored content import area (delve/imports/art, produced by scripts/extract-delver-reference.sh). 'tiles' is the default cell per role (the donor's t1 sheet). 'themes' paints a floor theme from its own donor atlas with weighted cell lists per role (index = column + row * columns; a cell listed n times is n times as likely), following the donor's texture painters (generator/<Theme>/info.dat texturePainters, generator/<Section>/section.dat level painters). Roles a theme leaves out keep the default cell. A theme's 'fog' is its donor section's linear fog (generator/<Section>/section.dat fogStart, fogEnd, fogColor) and applies with or without art. The art is donor-derived and never committed. Without staged art the level keeps its placeholder colors.",
